        "title": "World Heritage Site",
        "text": "This was an amazing experience and one i would recommend to anyone visiting Kathmandu. Non Hindus can't access some of the areas but we could see pretty much everything from the other side of the river. It is a very spiritual place but also seemed to be a place of celebration. Have your photo (for a small cost) taken with Holy Men who (we were told) enjoy smoking a bit of hash - they did seem mellow. You have the privilege of viewing cremations taking place. It is an experience I will never forget.",
