      {
        "review_id": 452481070,
        "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r452481070-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html",
        "title": "Amazing array of temples and interesting things to see.",
        "text": "If you are a bit squeamish then don't visit. There is a big Hindu Temple there and outside on the river bank are some large stone platforms where cremations are conducted, after the cremations the ashes are pushed into the river. We went in January which is Nepal's winter but there is no or little rain (the rains come mostly in the monsoon season) and so the river is not flowing so it is a dirty charcoal colour. There are many other buildings and small temples to look at. You could easily spend three hours there.We teamed up with a local guide at the entrance, or should I say he teamed up with us, but it was really worth the tip we gave him as he went into great detail about each building plus some history. I do wonder though about rituals still carried out today which to me should have been dispensed with centuries ago, for example there was a young goat tethered outside a small temple and when we inquired as to its purpose there we were informed it was to be slaughtered as an offering to the gods.",
        "review_tip": null,
