        "title": "No photo and shoes allowed!",
        "text": "This is one of the most renowned Hindu temples in South East Asia. It lies on the bank of Bagmati river. Visitors witness the journey of life and death at this place. There's no words to describe the experience of visiting Pashupatinath Temple. Highly spiritual place for people who believe in spirituality. Inside the temple people aren't allowed to take pictures for religious reasons. For the same reasons visitors must take off shoes and deposit it at shoes safety vault free of charge before entering the main temple premise. In the past the main temple was accessible for Hindus only but not sure if the same rule applies or not at the moment. This is one of my most favourite places to visit when I am in Kathmandu. ",
